btype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0131. The diff meets the goal and stays inside the contract and budget; my one reservation (the x2t point below) doesn't justify a rejection.\n\n**Rejection checks (TEP-0004)**\n- **Executor log:** filled in, with the decisions, the method and the surprise.\n- **Follow-ups:** one was requested. It isn't listed under \"Spawned packets\", but the file is in `.theseus/spawn/` (`PKT-0131-serve-integrated-make-x2t-run-the-integrated-sdk.md`), and the rule only requires one of the two.\n- **Characterize rule:** doesn't apply. This is a measure packet.\n- **Executor report:** it lists nothing the goal requires as left undone.\n\n**Goal**\n- **Runner script:** `convert-docx-pdf.sh` prints the required `total_ms/min_ms/max_ms/runs` line and runs against the integrated build by default.\n- **Map header and YAML:** the map has the right header and the YAML block. Every stage has `id`, `module`, `files`, `functions`, `ms` and `share`, and `unattributed_ms` is there.\n- **Totals:** the stages add up to 1209 ms against 1200 ms, well inside the 5% allowed.\n- **Large stages:** the only stage above 5% is x2t, and it names its functions. Its split into three parts comes from standalone runs and strace, and the map says so.\n- **Comparison with earlier rounds:** there is no earlier map of this journey, so the comparison is with `baseline.md`. The map says this openly, which is reasonable.\n- **Contract:** no project or fork code changed. Six files were changed, against a budget of 8.\n\n**Measurement method**\n- **Stage boundaries:** these come from the server's own debug logs, filtered by a key that is new on every run. Only log lines written after each run starts are read, so runs can't contaminate each other.\n- **Incomplete runs:** a run with a missing log mark is dropped from the stage medians, but its total still counts in `total_ms`. That is correct for the headline number. The script reports the count as `incomplete` on stderr.\n- **Download check:** the PDF must download with status 200 and be at least 1000 bytes. That's a weak check that the PDF is valid, but it is enough for a timing journey.\n\n**Weaknesses (none blocking)**\n- **The build x2t runs isn't fully integrated.** x2t loads the packaged snapshot `sdk-all.bin`, so 98% of the measured time runs the packaged editor code, not the forks' branch. This partly misses \"against the integrated build\". The executor:\n  - found it and wrote it up;\n  - ran an A/B comparison, where the gap was within noise;\n  - showed that a rebuilt snapshot gives similar timings;\n  - put the original snapshot back, byte-identical;\n  - asked for a high-priority follow-up to fix `serve-integrated.sh`.\n\n  `target.files` is empty, so changing that existing script was out of scope. I accept it on that basis, but the follow-up should be done before the next round's numbers are relied on.\n- **The integrated build is never taken down.** `convert-docx-pdf.sh` runs `serve-integrated.sh up` but not `down`, so the machine is left on the integrated build. This matches what the existing journey scripts appear to do.\n- **The poll stage is an artefact of the test.** It measures the 20 ms polling interval the runner chose, not the server. It is small and the map labels it that way.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE The journey is mapped with the required header, YAML and totals within 5%, the contract is kept, and the x2t snapshot problem is disclosed, A/B-checked and has a follow-up.","ttft_ms":3985,"type":"result","duration_ms":27348,"uuid":"0b4da6d8-96c7-4bea-aa86-df168afb7cb5","ttft_stream_ms":2358,"time_to_request_ms":315,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":184,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":17,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":10,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":5,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"r